# ============================================================
# Human-owned paths of the AI factory (backlog #0-113). The ruleset of main
# (.github/repository-settings/rulesets/main.json, ADR-0034) requires a code owner's review, so a PR touching
# any of these waits for the owner's approval of its last push. GitHub reads this file from main, not from the
# PR, so a PR cannot remove its own paths from it. The owner's own PRs merge through the ruleset's bypass (the
# admin role, at merge only): an author cannot approve their own PR.
#
# Shadow mode: the first line makes the owner the code owner of every path, so every PR, Renovate's and the
# owner's own included, needs the owner's approval. The ruleset's one required approval alone would not do:
# GitHub counts an approval from anyone with Write, and the autopilot's machine account could approve a PR it
# did not open (security review of #0-113). Phase 3 (docs/ai-factory.md) removes that line, after #0-153 decides
# which paths stay owned, so a PR touching none of the paths below can merge on its required checks alone.
#
# The owner must be a login GitHub can resolve: it ignores lines whose owner it cannot, and then nothing
# is protected. GitHub applies the last line that matches a path; every line names the owner.
# ============================================================

# Shadow mode: every path (removed in phase 3, #0-153)
